  "notes": "{生存|せいぞん} means survival or the state of being alive. It's commonly used in serious contexts like disasters, medical situations, and biology.\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {生存|せいぞん}{者|しゃ}: survivor\n- {生存|せいぞん}{率|りつ}: survival rate\n- {生存|せいぞん}{競争|きょうそう}: survival competition, struggle for existence\n- {生存|せいぞん}{確認|かくにん}: confirmation of survival (checking if someone is alive)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {生|い}きる: to live (verb)\n- {生命|せいめい}: life (biological)\n- サバイバル: survival (loanword, often for survival activities/shows)",
